<title>USA: Gulfstream Aerospace Q4 net income falls.</title>
<headline>Gulfstream Aerospace Q4 net income falls.</headline>
<dateline>SAVANNAH, Ga 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>GULFSTREAM AEROSPACE CORP</p>
<p>				  3 Mos ended 12/31  Year ended 12/31</p>
<p>					  1996   1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Net revenues			321.2  327.2  1,063.7  1,041.5</p>
<p> Gross profit			 59.3   64.9    224.5    206.0</p>
<p> Income from operations	   18.5   20.6     50.3     42.1</p>
<p> Net income			   14.4   18.9     47.0     28.9</p>
<p> Earnings per share (1) (2)     0.18   0.24     0.60     0.37</p>
<p>		  ($ in millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>Aircraft deliveries (in units):</p>
<p>    Green - GIV			  4	7	 24	 26</p>
<p>    Green - GV			   3	0	  3	  0</p>
<p>    Completion			  10     14	 27	 29</p>
<p>    Pre-owned aircraft		 6	7	 16	 21</p>
<p>NOTE: (1)  EPS calculated assuming the Company's IPO and related debt transactions that occurred during October 1996 had occurred as of the beginning of the reporting period, based on 78.5 million shares outstanding including the exercised overallotment.</p>
<p>(2)  Company recorded no provision for income taxes in 1995 and 1996, principally as a result of utilization of net operating loss carryforwards.</p>
<p>On a pro forma basis, assuming an effective tax rate of 37.5%, earnings per share would have been $0.37 and $0.23 for fiscal 1996 and 1995, and $0.11 and $0.15 for the quarters ended December 31, 1996 and 1995, respectively.</p>
</text>
